  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal gas initially at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ temperature, is compressed suddenly to one fourth of its volume. If the ratio of specific heat at constant pressure to that at constant volume is $3 / 2$, the change in temperature due to the thermodynamic process is _____ K."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "273",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\gamma=\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ & \\mathrm{Tv}^{\\gamma-1}=\\mathrm{C} \\\\ & 273 \\mathrm{~V}_0^{0.5}=\\mathrm{T}\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{V}_0}{4}\\right)^{0.5} \\\\ & \\mathrm{~T}=273 \\times 2=546 \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{~T}=273\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}